      "datastore_active": false,
      "description": "Camera image evaluation results for 7 x 3816 repetitions of the seven measurement scenarios presented in the manuscript (see extended data figure 1).\r\n\r\nEach line contains:\r\n* image number\r\n* measurement scenario number\r\n* camera count value mF=+1, after subtraction of systematic effects\r\n* camera count value mF=0, raw values\r\n* camera count value mF=-1, after subtraction of systematic effects\r\n* quantized atom number mF=+1\r\n* quantized atom number mF=0\r\n* quantized atom number mF=-1\r\n* camera count value mF=+1, raw values\r\n* camera count value mF=+1, raw values\r\n\r\nNote that for the mF=+/-1 camera count values two systematic effects were subtracted ('signal leakage' from mF=0 atoms and a drifting background value), as described in the Methods section. This is why the values are non-integers.",
